  "details": "I know there is another thread for this but this is just above normal...\nNormally 4gb is normal for vrchat (still a bit to much). I only joined 1 world for over 2 hours (The great pub), I rejoined because got blue screened because of memory management (probably the reason why I got blue screened). When I was monitoring it when I got a ingame lagg spike the ram spiked up and didn't go down.\nLagg spikes happend most time when people where changing avatars. I use custom safety settings only avatar & voice and nothing more, only for friend I have enabled everything.\nBut this is just extreem, 14gb of ram and won't go down, I play on desktop mode, for vr users this will be a big problem.\nI got a i9900ks, gtx 2070 super and 32gb of ddr4 ram.\n\nSince I read more threads this has been a issue since 2017?! Why not dedicating a lot of time fixing this instead working on a new sdk?",
